# Routing

Expo Router maps files in `src/app/` to routes, so the folder structure *is* the
navigation. Creating a file creates a screen.

- `src/app/(tabs)/` — the tab bar. A new file here adds a tab, so register it in
  `(tabs)/_layout.tsx` too. Parentheses group routes without appearing in the URL.
- `src/app/thing/[id].tsx` — a screen that takes a parameter, read with
  `useLocalSearchParams()`.
- `_layout.tsx` — shared shell for everything in its folder.

Conventions:

- Navigate with `<Link href={...}>` for anything a user taps. Use
  `router.push()` only for navigation triggered by code, such as after a form
  submits.
- Type route params: `useLocalSearchParams<{ id: string }>()`.
- Every dynamic screen must handle the case where its record does not exist.
- Keep route files thin. They compose components and fetch data; visual details
  belong in components.
